  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">GRZ- FN-gemensamt program mot k&#xf6;nsrelaterat       v&#xe5;ld</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GRZ-UN Joint Programme on GBV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme on gender based violence</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNDP har hos Sida ans&#xf6;kt om extra medel uppg&#xe5;ende till 30 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra GRZ-UN Joint P Program on Gender Based Violence in Zambia under perioden 2014 till 2016 (programmet startade 2012). Detta kommer att h&#xf6;ja det svenska bidraget till totalt 60 miljoner kronor. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att etablera en sektor&#xf6;verskridande mekanism f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av anti-GBV-lagen fr&#xe5;n 2011. Insatsens totala budget uppg&#xe5;r till cirka 104124000 kronor. FN bidrar med 13 miljoner kronor; Irish Aid bidrar mer 12,4 miljoner kronor.

The UNDP has applied for additional funding to SIDA of 30 million SEK to implement the GRZ-UN Joint Program on Gender Based Violence in Zambia during the period 2014 to 2016 (the program begun in 2012). This will bring the total Swedish Contribution to 60 million SEK.

The overall objective of the intervention is to establish an integrated and multi-sectoral mechanism for the implementation of the Anti-GBV Act of 2011. The intervention&apos;s total budget is approximately SEK102 506 698 000. The UN are contributing SEK 13 000 000; the Irish Aid is contributing SEK12,400,000.</narrative>
  </description>
